{
  "name": "Oriel",
  "_about": "AN ORIEL (Erker): a three-sided bay `w` wide at the wall and `d` deep, its slanted faces coming in `c`, `H` tall from its floor (the placement, on the wall's face, +z out), carried on a stepped corbel `foot` deep below it; a pointed window in each face (winW, from sill to spring), a sill course and a cornice; `cap` helm puts a slate helm `capRise` tall over it, `cap` flat a parapet parH high round a flat top.",
